# Flutter UI Builder

## What This Skill Does
Generates correctly structured Flutter UI code that follows project
conventions — theming, widget decomposition, state handling, and
performance patterns.

## Widget Structure Rules

### Always private widget classes, never helper methods
```dart
// Correct — private class
class _TaskCard extends StatelessWidget {
  const _TaskCard({required this.task});
  final Task task;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => ...;
}

// Wrong — private method returning Widget
Widget _buildTaskCard(Task task) => ...;
```

### Break large build() methods into private classes
Any `build()` method over 40 lines should be broken into named private
widget classes. Each class should have a single, clear visual responsibility.

### Use const wherever possible
```dart
// Correct
const SizedBox(height: 16),
const Divider(),
const Text('Hello'),

// Wrong — missing const
SizedBox(height: 16),
```

## Theming — Never Hardcode Colors or Text Styles

```dart
// Correct
color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.primary,
color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.surface,
color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.onSurface,
style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.titleMedium,
style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.bodySmall,

// Wrong
color: Colors.blue,
color: const Color(0xFF1976D2),
style: const TextStyle(fontSize: 14),
```

## Color Scheme Reference

| Token | Use for |
|---|---|
| `colorScheme.primary` | Primary actions, active states |
| `colorScheme.onPrimary` | Text/icons on primary color |
| `colorScheme.surface` | Card and container backgrounds |
| `colorScheme.onSurface` | Primary text on surface |
| `colorScheme.surfaceVariant` | Subtle container backgrounds |
| `colorScheme.outline` | Borders, dividers |
| `colorScheme.error` | Error states only |
| `colorScheme.tertiary` | Accent highlights (streaks, points) |

## Common Widget Patterns

### Screen scaffold
```dart
class TaskCreateScreen extends ConsumerWidget {
  const TaskCreateScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    ref.listen(taskCreateControllerProvider, (_, state) {
      if (state.hasError) {
        ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
          SnackBar(content: Text(state.error.toUserMessage())),
        );
      }
      if (!state.isLoading && !state.hasError) context.pop();
    });

    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(title: const Text('New Task')),
      body: const SafeArea(
        child: SingleChildScrollView(
          padding: EdgeInsets.all(16),
          child: _TaskCreateForm(),
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

### AsyncValue rendering — always all three states
```dart
ref.watch(tasksForDateProvider).when(
  data:    (tasks) => _TaskList(tasks: tasks),
  loading: () => const _TaskListSkeleton(),
  error:   (e, _) => _ErrorCard(message: e.toUserMessage()),
);
```

### List — always builder, never Column + map
```dart
// Correct — lazy loaded
ListView.builder(
  itemCount: tasks.length,
  itemBuilder: (context, index) => _TaskCard(task: tasks[index]),
)

// Wrong — builds all at once
Column(
  children: tasks.map((t) => _TaskCard(task: t)).toList(),
)
```

### Empty state
```dart
class _EmptyState extends StatelessWidget {
  const _EmptyState({required this.message});
  final String message;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Center(
    child: Column(
      mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,
      children: [
        Icon(
          Icons.inbox_outlined,
          size: 48,
          color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.outline,
        ),
        const SizedBox(height: 12),
        Text(
          message,
          style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.bodyMedium?.copyWith(
            color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.outline,
          ),
        ),
      ],
    ),
  );
}
```

### Loading skeleton
```dart
class _TaskListSkeleton extends StatelessWidget {
  const _TaskListSkeleton();

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => ListView.builder(
    itemCount: 5,
    padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16),
    itemBuilder: (_, __) => const _TaskCardSkeleton(),
  );
}

class _TaskCardSkeleton extends StatelessWidget {
  const _TaskCardSkeleton();

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Container(
    margin: const EdgeInsets.only(bottom: 12),
    height: 72,
    decoration: BoxDecoration(
      color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.surfaceVariant,
      borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12),
    ),
  );
}
```

## Spacing — Use Consistent Values

Always use multiples of 4:
```dart
// Standard spacing values
const double s4  = 4;
const double s8  = 8;
const double s12 = 12;
const double s16 = 16;
const double s24 = 24;
const double s32 = 32;

// Usage
const SizedBox(height: 16),
const EdgeInsets.all(16),
const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 24, vertical: 12),
```

## Performance Rules
- Always `const` on widgets with no dynamic data.
- Always `ListView.builder` for lists — never `Column` with `.map()`.
- Use `select()` on providers to avoid unnecessary rebuilds.
- Never do computation inside `build()` — move to controller or domain extension.

## Rules
- Never hardcode colors — always `Theme.of(context).colorScheme`.
- Never hardcode text styles — always `Theme.of(context).textTheme`.
- Always use private widget classes, never private widget methods.
- Always handle loading and error states — never assume data is available.
- Always use `SafeArea` on root screen widgets.
- Always use `ListView.builder` for any list of variable length.
- Always pass explicit keys to list item widgets when items can reorder.
